# Derpseek wavefront-fast (v0): lossy-fast, and in a decode step a CPU-memory expert that would make a MoE call wait costs
# precision for that step, never time. Per call in layers 20-38 the distinct host-row experts beyond a small window
# (1 at up to 8 rows, 2 to 16, 3 to 32, 5 to 64) are skipped for the step, weakest first by the summed rank of their
# picks, never an expert holding one of a token's two strongest picks, and at most 4% of the band's picks per step (beyond
# that the call reads them as in exact). A skipped expert still counts as a miss, so it is promoted for the next steps.
# One small kernel between the router and MegaMoE (derpseek_engine/cutk.py). Decode-path KLD 0.0296 (lossy-fast 0.0281).
# The bit-plane form (low-precision bases in GPU memory, refinements over the link) does not fit: 2-plane bases of a
# layer's non-static experts need 2.2 GB against its 1.8 GB cache (Fable round 20); this is its zero-bit base.
. "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/lossy-fast.env"
export DERPSEEK_MISS=cut
export DERPSEEK_MISS_LAYERS=${DERPSEEK_MISS_LAYERS:-20-38}
